// ===================== 15.5 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('15.5  The note to the keeper'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Three facts, and the third is the one that matters: how many times did the keeper mention it?** **In this room neither keeper mentioned it once in two years.** **The eight without envelopes name the person who holds the file they read in 15.4** — **a clerk, an officer, a night editor** — **and that is the same relationship in a different shape, because they too hold something about the writer and have never discussed it.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Belong: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **2 is the content; 4 names an act.** **1, 3 and 5 are thanks with nothing in them** — _it meant a great deal_, _you will be pleased to know_, _I hope it was not too much trouble_ — **and the room should be made to say what act each one names, which is none.** **The answer the room will give is _keeping it_** — **and thanks for keeping a letter is thanks for not reading it, which is not a service anybody can be congratulated for.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **the content.** **A keeper who carried a document for two years has a claim on knowing what it said** — **and a note that thanks them and does not tell them has treated a person as a safe.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **He wrote the date of handing it over on the back, in his own hand, and did not mention it.**   **2** ⚠ **It is thanks for not reading something.** **What he actually did was two things: he kept it where he could find it, and he wrote the date on the back** — **and a note that names neither has thanked him for a quality rather than an act.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the cycle where the unit stops being about the writer, and the room will resist it harder than anything else in Book 2 so far.** **Nine of ten first drafts opened with thanks and not one of the nine named an act.** **The instruction is mechanical: the content comes first, the thanks come once at the end, and the thanks name an act or they do not appear.** **If a student cannot name an act, the honest draft has no thanks in it at all** — **and the room will find that unbearable, which is the point at which to say that a note with no thanks and a full account is more respectful than the reverse.** ⚠ **And the judgement about which sentences the keeper gets is a judgement and not a rule.** **The test is whether a sentence was a claim.** **A claim was always going to be settled by the world and a keeper is part of the world** — **and the sentences about what the writer wanted are of no use to anybody else.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **The claim, and what settled it** — _the third sentence was a prediction that nobody from here gets an answer; four answers came between March and November._   **2** **The act nobody asked for** — _you wrote the date of handing it over on the back._   **3** **Thanks, once, at the end** — **and for that act and no other.**   **4** ⚠ **A keeper who holds a file** — _eleven letters with no apology, and the date of the last._ **They have had it in a drawer without knowing it was information.**   **5** ⚠ **A sentence you are not going to tell them** — **and say that you are not.**'));
