out.push(SAMPLE(['Mr Attar thought the note to Mr Deeb should be thanks and he was wrong, and Mrs Oueidat asked him what he was thanking him for and he could not answer it in a way that was about Mr Deeb. Mrs Oueidat said thanks for keeping a letter is thanks for not reading it, which is not a service anybody can be congratulated for, and what he actually did was two things: he kept it where he could find it, and he wrote the date of handing it over on the back. Dr Qabbani said and the second one nobody asked for, and nobody asked and he did not mention it: he wrote the date in his own hand and gave it over without comment, and the two dates together are the only part of the exercise that could not have been arranged afterwards. Mrs Khoury said so the note tells him what was in it, because a keeper who has carried a document for two years has a claim on knowing what it said, and a note that thanks them and does not tell them has treated a person as a safe. Mrs Tarabishi asked whether all four sentences, and the one that was evidence and what settled it, not all four and not a summary of the writer. Mr Tayara asked whether he is not entitled to the private ones, and he is entitled to nothing and it is a judgement and not a rule: the test is whether a sentence was a claim. Mrs Ajouz asked where the thanks go, and once, at the end, and for the specific thing. Mrs Rizk said hers is a clerk who holds a file and does not know she read it, and then the note is better and harder, because she tells her what the file showed. Mr Zahreddine asked whether anybody replies, and Mr Deeb replied in two lines and said he had wondered what was in it and had decided not to ask. And Mr Attar said the thing he will take away is that he had wondered: he had thought of Mr Deeb as a place he had put something, and he is the only other person who knew the letter existed. Mrs Khoury said that is the sentence the cycle is for, because a keeper is a party to the exercise and every draft in the room had treated one as a container. Mrs Oueidat said the two notes that went were both answered and both replies contained something the writer had not known. And Mrs Rizk said the thing she will take away is that her clerk has had the information in a drawer for nine months without knowing it was information.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the one to carry out of the cycle and it must not be softened into gratitude: he had thought of Mr Deeb as a place he had put something.** **It is a finding about who else was in the exercise.** **Mr Deeb was the only other person who knew the letter existed, and for most of two years he was the only one at all** — **because the writer had forgotten about it from the following spring until the end of November.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **Thanks in the first line** → **nine of ten first drafts, and none named an act.**   **2** _Thank you for keeping it_ → **thanks for not reading something.**   **3** ⚠ **A silent withholding** → **the keeper cannot tell a short letter from a short extract.**   **4** _You will be pleased to know_ → **telling a keeper how to feel about a document they have not read.**   **5** ⚠ **The summary of the writer instead of the claim** → **the keeper is being asked to be interested in the writer.**   **6** **No question at all** → **the keeper has been a party to this for two years with no part in it.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **He tells him the claim and what settled it: the prediction and the four answers, with the date of the earliest.** **He withholds the other three, which were about what he wanted at twenty** — **and he says that he is withholding them and why: they were not claims about the world, nothing could have settled them, and handing them over would be asking Mr Deeb to be interested in him.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **Either date alone is one he could have written at any time; the two together, in two hands, cannot have been arranged afterwards.** **He names it as a property of Mr Deeb\'s handwriting and not of his letter** — **which is the sentence that makes the note about the keeper.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **For writing the date on the back, and he says it is the only thing he is thanking him for.** **It comes at the end, after the content** — **and 15.7 corrects the reason he gives for it, because it is the registry\'s routine and not a kindness, and Mr Deeb says so himself.**'));
