out.push(A('⚠ **Part 3 is the hardest listening part at this level because every option is said by somebody and the question is who.** **At 1 accept only B**: _that is a rule, written in the office_, **and candidates who choose A have heard _twenty years_ in the question before it.** **At 2 the answer is the woman\'s own reason** — _I would write the date for anybody who brought me anything_ — **and C is tempting because she does mention what she is permitted to do, but about a different thing.** ⚠ **At 3 she says plainly _it is never a good month_, and A is wrong on her own words: _I have no power to refuse anything_.** **At 5 she names the cabinet and both the things she is not permitted to do, so B is contradicted in the same sentence that makes it tempting.** **At 6 the whole last answer is the key** — _it is worth doing and not for the reason people do it_ — **and B is a true statement she makes earlier about keepers, which is why it is there.**'));
